---
// AI shipped into products: heading on top, then prose beside the matching pipeline (a hairline schematic)
---

<section id="ai" class="section" aria-labelledby="ai-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="ai-heading" class="h-section ai-heading">AI engineering</h2>
    <div class="ai-cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          I don't just use AI to write code. <strong
            >I ship AI inside the product&nbsp;— and make it behave.</strong
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          The AI features I've built run in production for real users: chat support on OpenAI
          that handles profile completion, job-matching questions, and referral guidance — and a
          matching pipeline where jobs and candidates become embeddings, Qdrant does the vector
          search, and scored matches flow back into the platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          Production AI is boundary engineering. A model is an unreliable dependency like any
          other, so the real work lives at the edges: structured outputs validated before they
          touch data, fallbacks for when the model is wrong or slow, and observability so a bad
          answer is a bug report instead of a mystery.
        </p>
        <p class="quiet">
          Currently going deeper down the stack — RAG pipelines, embedding strategy, and
          self-hosted models.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="plan card reveal">
        <figcaption class="sr-only">
          The matching pipeline: jobs and candidates are embedded via OpenAI, searched in Qdrant,
          and scored matches ship to production.
        </figcaption>
        <div class="flow" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="inputs">
            <span class="node">job post</span>
            <span class="node">candidate</span>
          </div>
          <span class="merge"></span>
          <span class="wire"></span>
          <div class="node">openai<span class="sub">embeddings</span></div>
          <span class="wire"></span>
          <div class="node">qdrant<span class="sub">vector search</span></div>
          <div class="tap">
            <p class="note">similarity, not keyword matching</p>
          </div>
          <div class="node">
            chat support <span class="sub">(openai)</span>
            <ul class="branches">
              <li>profile completion</li>
              <li>job-match questions</li>
              <li>referral guidance</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <span class="wire wire--ship"><span class="wire-label">ship</span></span>
          <div class="node node--dest">
            production
            <span class="live"><span class="dot"></span>live</span>
          </div>
          <p class="touchdown">real users, every day</p>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai-heading {
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.75rem, 1.25rem + 2vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* stacked, then prose | pipeline; the schematic holds its place while the prose scrolls */
  .ai-cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem 4rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .ai-cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .plan {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 2rem);
    }
  }

  .prose p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .prose .lede {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lede);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .lede strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.15em;
  }

  .prose .quiet {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  /* stacked, the card hugs the diagram instead of spanning the column */
  .plan {
    max-width: 30rem;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(0.875rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 24rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  /* caps = a stage in the flow, lowercase = detail */
  .node {
    width: min(100%, 15rem);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .sub,
  .branches {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* a sub-label alone in its node sits under the name; beside a branch list it stays inline */
  .sub:only-child {
    display: block;
  }

  /* two sources merge into one trunk */
  .inputs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    justify-items: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .inputs .node {
    width: auto;
  }

  .merge {
    width: 50%;
    height: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .wire {
    position: relative;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--line-strong);
  }

  /* arrowheads: a small step brighter than the hairline so the direction reads */
  .wire::after,
  .tap::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    width: 7px;
    height: 5px;
    translate: -50% 0;
    background: var(--text-faint);
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 50% 100%);
  }

  /* trunk segment that carries the annotation pinned to the qdrant node */
  .tap {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    width: 100%;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .tap::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: 0;
    left: calc(50% - 0.5px);
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--line-strong);
  }

  .note {
    grid-column: 2;
    position: relative;
    margin-left: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* dashed leader ending in a square pin on the node's edge */
  .note::before,
  .note::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    translate: -50% 0;
  }

  .note::before {
    top: 0;
    height: 0.85rem;
    border-left: 1px dashed var(--text-faint);
  }

  .note::after {
    top: -3px;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    background: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .branches {
    margin: 0.55rem 0 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .branches li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .branches li::before,
  .branches li::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    background: var(--line-strong);
  }

  .branches li::before {
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
  }

  .branches li:last-child::before {
    bottom: auto;
    height: 0.75em;
  }

  .branches li::after {
    top: 0.75em;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 1px;
  }

  .wire--ship {
    height: 2.5rem;
  }

  .wire-label {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 0.75rem;
    translate: 0 -55%;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .node--dest {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }

  /* the only lime in this section */
  .live {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .live .dot {
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
  }

  .touchdown {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
</style>
